From 664f697e80a1e9f4ab397a04a7b2d14d55f685e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKenzie Pepper <mapepp2@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:37:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] lavfi/qsvvpp: seed output surface timestamp from the
 input

MFX writes the output surface's Data.TimeStamp itself for most VPP operations,
but composition (mfxExtVPPComposite) leaves it untouched. ff_qsvvpp_filter_frame
then unconditionally overwrites the frame pts with that stale value, clobbering
the correct pts query_frame() had already copied from propref.

The result on a padded composite pipeline is a pts sequence of 0,0,0,0,1,2,3,4
instead of 0,512,1024,... The frame rate converter sees non-advancing
timestamps and drops nearly every frame: 2 of 120 survive to the muxer, while
-fps_mode passthrough shows all 120 frames were produced correctly all along.

Seeding the output timestamp from the input before RunFrameVPPAsync fixes it and
is a no-op wherever MFX supplies its own timestamp.
---
 libavfilter/qsvvpp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavfilter/qsvvpp.c b/libavfilter/qsvvpp.c
index c3685f1..60195ee 100644
--- a/libavfilter/qsvvpp.c
+++ b/libavfilter/qsvvpp.c
@@ -1000,6 +1000,14 @@ int ff_qsvvpp_filter_frame(QSVVPPContext *s, AVFilterLink *inlink, AVFrame *picr
         if (ret)
             return ret;
 
+        /* Seed the output timestamp from the input. Most VPP operations have
+         * MFX write the output surface's TimeStamp itself, in which case this
+         * is overwritten and costs nothing; but composition (mfxExtVPPComposite)
+         * leaves it untouched, and the stale value then clobbers the correct pts
+         * that query_frame() copied from propref -- which makes the frame rate
+         * converter drop nearly every frame as non-advancing. */
+        out_frame->surface.Data.TimeStamp = in_frame->surface.Data.TimeStamp;
+
         do {
             ret = MFXVideoVPP_RunFrameVPPAsync(s->session, &in_frame->surface,
                                                &out_frame->surface, NULL, &sync);
-- 
